From a086bcd4b58856ae613488db62c25bf8b63ba81b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:01:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] feat(mcp): add dashboard-create-with-insights with
 compensating rollback

One call creates a dashboard and all of its insight tiles. Job 1 of the
2026-11-10 friction session (five tiles and a reorder) took
dashboard-create, five insight-create calls, three prescribed
re-queries, an info and a reorder, with an 11,175-token reorder echo.

- Validate before writing anything: each new tile's query is checked
  against insight-create's own query schema and, with validate: "run"
  (the default), run once through the query API (the source of a
  visualization node, not the wrapper); each existing insight is read,
  and a duplicate is refused. Any failure lists every failing tile and
  creates nothing.
- Then create the dashboard and the tiles in order: a new insight
  created onto the dashboard, or an existing insight attached through a
  version-checked update of its `dashboards` list. `layout` arranges the
  tiles with the reorder endpoint in the given order.
- If a later step fails, a CompensationLog (compensation.ts) undoes what
  this call wrote, newest first: created insights and the dashboard are
  soft-deleted, attached insights are detached again. The error names
  the failed step, what was rolled back and anything that could not be.
  The REST API has no transaction, so the description says other readers
  can briefly see the partial dashboard.
- The receipt is trimmed to the dashboard id, name and url, and per tile
  its position, insight id, short_id and tile id. Tile ids come from the
  insights' own dashboard_tiles, so no dashboard re-read is needed.
- dry_run validates and returns the plan without writing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
